  "body": "## What changed\n\nAdd a shared public ownership procedure under `issue-claims`. Wire `work-issue`, `review-prs`, `resolve-conflicts` and `merge-ready` to it.\n\n- Record the writer with the issue claim and the reviewer on the PR.\n- Name the unique worker, dispatcher, branch, PR, base and exact starting head.\n- Read the records before dispatch and immediately before a push.\n- Stand down on observed live owners. Stop on moved heads or rejected pushes.\n- Preserve the local review lock, claim lifetimes and refresh timing.\n- Require `cargo check --tests` for affected code before a refresh push, including clean merges.\n\nThis is a cooperative procedure, not an atomic distributed lock. Concurrent comments and a race after the last read remain possible. The tests pin the instructions, not distributed exclusion. The decision file records the alternatives and these limits.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo test -p xtask ownership_contract_tests -- --nocapture`: four contract tests passed.\n  - `ownership_dispatch_paths_load_the_shared_guard`\n  - `ownership_record_and_lifecycle_contract`\n  - `ownership_stop_and_non_atomic_limits_are_explicit`\n  - `ownership_refresh_checks_precede_push_and_preserve_merge_validation`\n- The dispatch test failed before the four skill links were added. It passed after the change.\n- `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=3 cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: passed on this final tree. The recorded base was `bd467a0ccf581f3f700209247b62e6949ab7735e`. One real xtask step ran in 256 seconds: 399 tests passed across 12 test targets. No tests failed or were ignored.\n- `cargo check --tests -p xtask`: passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings`: blocked by existing `clippy::needless_bool` at `xtask/src/unit_sweep.rs:67`. That file matches the base. With only that lint allowed, the same check passed.\n- `rustfmt --edition 2021 --check xtask/src/ownership_contract_tests.rs`: passed. Package-wide `cargo fmt --check -p xtask` reports existing formatting differences; no broad formatting changes were made.\n- Relative Markdown links, code fences, final newlines, exact file scope and added-line security scan: passed.\n- `git diff --check`: passed.\n\nNo application, GUI, catalog-generation, light, heavy or release lane ran for this process-only change. No production CAM code, dependencies or workflow files changed. The quick step does run xtask's existing catalog-tool tests with synthetic fixtures. No maintainer runner was used.\n\nThe first quick command and a separate full xtask command hit a 240-second terminal limit. The complete quick rerun above passed. A slow existing reach-map test exceeded 60 seconds.\n\n## Ownership and scope\n\nWriter record: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/3661#issuecomment-7185068834\n\nThe branch starts from upstream main at the recorded base. Upstream advanced in unrelated files after branching. The published diff contains only the nine intended files. No refresh was needed.\n\nThe authenticated rules and rulesets endpoints returned empty lists. Legacy protection and required-check endpoints returned 404, not an empty success. No CI pass is inferred from absent checks.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: medium\nProcess change: yes\n\nFixes #3661\n",
